 "text": "Hi, how are you doing these days? About eye level with your sitting or standing height. Too low and you strain your neck, too high and you look like a giant. About three times the length of your van on each side. Less if you park near a wall or obstacle, more if there' lots of space. Then pick a monitor stand that's tall enough and move it as close as it safely can. A monitor bracket that screws into the wall is nice too. Textbooks are great for height and weight. A thick book on table is about right for a typical desk.",
